# Shell scripts and the Python scripts they drive run under Linux (WSL, CI
# containers). A CRLF working-tree copy breaks them at the first line:
# bash reads the \r as part of the command ("$'\r': command not found").
# Force LF regardless of each contributor's core.autocrlf setting.
*.sh text eol=lf
security/scripts/*.py text eol=lf
